Z||000000||LAMBO||09-08-2000||11:24 AM||||Called the parts store today to get a price on a timing chain set for an 86 2.8 V6. They said there were two different sets available for that year and engine depending on the engine code (whether its a W or and F). What's up with that? Why in the heck would Pontiac have two different applications for the same motor in the same year. Does it have to do with an auto vs. manual? Did they change cams halfway through the production year? Anyone know?<BR>Lambo ||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-08-2000||01:00 PM||||Maybe you need to call another parts store.<BR>Engine code for Fiero 2.8 V6 is "9," I think.  <BR> <BR>"W" and "F" are for 3800 engine - I think. ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||09-08-2000||06:52 PM||||The 'W' block is the same block as the '9'. you are safe if you go that way. I'm with Stu though, go some place where they know what they're looking for! The 'F' block is very different, all three (9, W & F) are 2.8's.||||reg||1
Z||000003||LAMBO||09-08-2000||11:34 PM||||Thanks guys. Called NAPA and got it straight this time. Gonna cost me a little more but at least I know what I'm getting.<BR>Todd||||reg||1
